        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It’s an automation script that helps to create Firefox release notes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I created the <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41896\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41896/hovercard\">Firefox 145 release notes PR</a> using this script.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To simplify release notes workflow.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How it works, for example, with the newly released Firefox 145:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"node scripts/release-firefox.js 145\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">node scripts/release-firefox.js 145</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What it does:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Takes the newly released version as a parameter (N), and:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Removes active from N-1</li>\n<li>Updates N to Stable\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Uncomments HTML, CSS, JavaScript “no notable changes” sections</li>\n<li>Removes all other unused commented sections</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Updates N+1 to Beta</li>\n<li>Adds Nightly N+2 page</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For release dates, it uses official JSON API — <a href=\"https://whattrainisitnow.com/api/firefox/calendar/future/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://whattrainisitnow.com/api/firefox/calendar/future/</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3610323814\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41896\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41896/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41896\">#41896</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41897",
            "title": "Add Firefox release automation script",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-11T08:42:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-11T01:47:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The \"Visual Viewport API\" sidebar has been removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3267000779\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40547\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40547/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40547\">#40547</a>. This PR removes the last remnant, which is the landing page, by subsuming its information into <code class=\"notranslate\">VisualViewport</code>. It also removes links to a nonexistent API \"Viewport API\". I'm not sure how this even got into MDN: perhaps the <code class=\"notranslate\">Viewport</code> interface was meant.</p>",
